{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773244698,"nonce":"iEJNoGLxYMFhTc4p/lDMTCmOFrs=","title":"Review step: automated code review before human review","message":"Implement an automated review step that runs after the coder finishes, before notifying the human.\n\n## Design\n\nThe reviewer is a standard nightshift session — same Docker image, same session runner, same markers — but with a different config file (REVIEW.md) and its own worktree (clean clone from the agent branch).\n\n### Flow\n\n1. Coder finishes → status `waiting:review`\n2. Watcher detects `waiting:review`, checks if REVIEW.md exists in the repo\n3. If REVIEW.md exists:\n   a. Create a fresh worktree from the agent branch (e.g. `review/{sid}`)\n   b. Launch a new nightshift session with `--workflow REVIEW.md`\n   c. Coder session status → `reviewing`\n4. Reviewer runs in a clean container:\n   - Install deps from scratch\n   - Run tests (configured in REVIEW.md)\n   - Read diff (base..agent branch)\n   - Evaluate code quality, test results, adherence to requirements\n   - Post verdict as tracker comment\n5. Reviewer finishes (@@DONE@@):\n   - If satisfied: posts `@nightshift approve` → status `waiting:human-review` → notify human\n   - If not: posts `@nightshift revise` with feedback → coder resumes\n6. If no REVIEW.md → current behavior (notify human directly)\n\n### Session naming\n\nSessions support a step prefix to distinguish coder from reviewer:\n- Coder: `agent/{sid}` branch, `.nightshift/sessions/{sid}/` session dir\n- Reviewer: `review/{sid}` branch, `.nightshift/sessions/review-{sid}/` session dir\n\nThis generalizes to `{step}/{sid}` for future pipeline steps.\n\n### New statuses\n\n- `reviewing` — reviewer is running\n- `waiting:human-review` — reviewer approved, awaiting human confirmation\n\n### New command\n\n- `@nightshift approve` — reviewer is satisfied, escalate to human\n\n### REVIEW.md\n\nSame format as WORKFLOW.md (YAML front matter + Jinja2 prompt template):\n\n```yaml\n---\nagent:\n  kind: claude-code    # or codex, etc.\n  max_turns: 10\n  \nworkspace:\n  kind: worktree\n  base_branch: master  # will be overridden to agent branch\n  root: .worktrees\n\nmax_rounds: 3          # max reviewer ↔ coder cycles before escalating\n---\n\nYou are reviewing code changes for the following issue:\n\n**Title:** {{ issue.title }}\n**Description:**\n{{ issue.body }}\n\n**Diff ({{ base_branch }}..{{ agent_branch }}):**\n```\n{{ diff }}\n```\n\n**Test command:** Run `python -m pytest tests/` and report results.\n\n## Instructions\n1. Run the test suite first\n2. Review the diff for correctness, style, and completeness\n3. Check that changes match the issue requirements\n4. If tests fail or code needs changes: @@DONE@@ then post @nightshift revise with specific feedback\n5. If everything looks good: @@DONE@@ then post @nightshift approve\n```\n\n### Implementation scope\n\n- Watcher: add `reviewing` state handling, launch reviewer on `waiting:review` if REVIEW.md exists\n- launch.py: support `--step review` flag for session/branch naming\n- Prompt: inject diff and test results into REVIEW.md template\n- New `approve` command that transitions to `waiting:human-review`\n- `max_rounds` tracking in watcher\n\n### Future evolution\n\nThis is a hardcoded two-step pipeline (coder → reviewer). The architecture supports upgrading to:\n1. PIPELINE.md defining step ordering\n2. LLM orchestrator that decides next step dynamically\n\nEach step remains a standard nightshift session — the only thing that changes is who decides which session to launch next.","files":null}]}